  "subject_group": null,
  "versions": [
    {
      "designator": "CS23-0",
      "grouping_at_time": "Subpart C \u2014 Structure",
      "title_at_revision": "Unsymmetrical flight conditions",
      "text": "(See AMC 23.347 (b))\n(a) The aeroplane is assumed to be subjected to the unsymmetrical flight conditions of CS 23.349 and 23.351. Unbalanced aerodynamic moments about the centre of gravity must be reacted in a rational or conservative manner, considering the principal masses furnishing the reacting inertia forces.\n(b) Aerobatic category aeroplanes certified for flick manoeuvres (snap-roll) must be designed for additional asymmetric loads acting on the wing and the horizontal tail.",
